<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n13064" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dē-mulcĕo</span></b> , lsi,
			mulctum, 2, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. a., to stroke down, to stroke caressingly</i>
			(rare). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Prop.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">caput tibi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ter.
					Heaut. 4, 5, 14</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dorsum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv. 9,
					16 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aures, Lact. de Ira, 7, 9: crura,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell. 5, 14, 12</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>to soften,
			allure</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aures omnium mentesque demulsit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell. 16, 19, 6</span></i>
			; cf.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ita motus et demulctus et captus est, ut, etc.,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 3,
					13 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">eum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					18, 2, 1</span></i>
			.</div>
